# The image's build context (Dockerfile): the platform code and the page, the simulated estate's generator, the
# meta-model, the platform's preloaded standards, the Makefile, the requirements, the entry script and the legal notices, and nothing else. Everything is
# left out first and each of those let back in; then what no image may hold is left out again, wherever it sits. So no
# client's pack or deployment (clients/, deploy/), no build (build/: the estate, the graphs, the tokens), no tests,
# no .env, no key and no Python cache reaches the build.
*
!Makefile
!meta-model.yaml
!requirements.txt
!constraints.txt
!entrypoint.sh
!pyproject.toml
!LICENSE
!THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
!kge
!standards
!ui
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/tokens.json
**/passwords*
**/credentials.json
**/secrets.yaml
